From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:15:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820: Add the Mali-G76 GPU

Describe the Mali-G76 MP12 GPU, so panfrost can drive it.  On this
phone GPU_ID reads 0x72110000 and SHADER_PRESENT 0x00770077, with one
L2 cache group.

The firmware on the APM owns the clock and the voltage of the GPU, so
its clock is the ACPM DVFS domain.  There are no operating points yet:
the GPU runs at the level the firmware starts it at, 156 MHz, and no
DVFS message goes to the firmware.

The power domain of the GPU is left out.  The bootloader leaves it on,
and around every power cycle of it the vendor kernel saves and restores
the TrustZone protection setup of the block with an SMC, which the
Exynos power domain driver does not do.  How the block comes back
without that restore has not been tested.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi
index 69826c4f3aa..2d7d2007c0b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820.dtsi
@@ -953,6 +953,25 @@ hsi2c45: i2c@15d60000 {
 			};
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * A Mali-G76 MP12: GPU_ID reads 0x72110000 and SHADER_PRESENT
+		 * 0x00770077 on this phone.  The firmware on the APM owns its clock
+		 * and voltage, and with no operating points the GPU stays at the
+		 * level the firmware starts it at.  The power domain is left out:
+		 * the bootloader leaves it on, and the vendor saves and restores
+		 * the TrustZone setup of the block with an SMC around every power
+		 * cycle, which the power domain driver does not do.
+		 */
+		gpu: gpu@18500000 {
+			compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-mali", "arm,mali-bifrost";
+			reg = <0x18500000 0x5000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 288 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 287 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 289 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupt-names = "job", "mmu", "gpu";
+			clocks = <&acpm_ipc EXYNOS9820_CLK_ACPM_DVFS_G3D>;
+		};
+
 		pinctrl_aud: pinctrl@18c60000 {
 			compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-pinctrl";
 			reg = <0x18c60000 0x1000>;
